Fix the map painting over the panels on phones

Leaflet gives its panes z-index 400 and up, and #map was positioned with
z-index auto, so it created no stacking context. Those panes competed
directly with the rail and slip at z-index 80 and won. The side panel was
opening on every tap of the hamburger - it was just being painted over by
the map. The map wrapper now isolates its own stacking context.

The overlay canvas is also pinned to the map container and drawn in
container coordinates, instead of being repositioned against the moving
pane each frame. That removes the offset band seen on mobile.

With the header tabs hidden below 900px there was no way to reach Layers,
Access, Regs or Log on a phone; the panel now carries its own tabs and a
close button, and choosing one no longer slams the drawer shut. The map key
starts closed on narrow screens, where it covered most of the map.

Satellite native zoom capped at 18 so zoom 19 upscales rather than asking
Esri for rural tiles that do not exist.

